## 3.10 Traceability

### Purpose

The Traceability section establishes the documented links between a System Objective and the engineering artifacts that govern, derive from, verify, validate, or otherwise reference it.

Its purpose is to ensure complete engineering traceability throughout the lifecycle of the objective.

---

### Standard Fields

Every System Objective shall include the following fields:

| Field | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| Parent Governing Document | Governing document authorizing the objective. |
| Source Reference | Source from which the objective originates, where applicable. |
| Derived Requirements | Requirements derived from the objective. |
| Architectural References | Architecture documents implementing or supporting the objective. |
| Verification References | Verification artifacts linked to the objective. |
| Validation References | Validation artifacts linked to the objective. |
| Related Engineering Records | Other approved engineering records associated with the objective. |

---

### Traceability Rules

Traceability shall:

- Be maintained throughout the objective lifecycle.
- Reference only approved engineering artifacts.
- Preserve bidirectional traceability where required.
- Be updated whenever linked artifacts change.
- Support engineering audits and impact analysis.

---

### Engineering Note

Traceability enables engineers to understand how a System Objective is connected to the wider AVIA engineering ecosystem.

It supports change impact analysis, verification planning, validation activities, and long-term repository integrity.
